7
00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:38.800
My daughter, he said, "What are you doing?

8
00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:43.580
The thought of yourself makes you go out of my will.

9
00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:50.680
This is extremely important for us, that all our self-reflection pulls us out of the divine

10
00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:51.680
will.

11
00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:59.080
If we are locked into the divine will, then we are having his thought, and we're responding

12
00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:02.200
to him, not to ourselves.

13
00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:06.360
The thought of yourself makes you go out of my will.

14
00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:12.520
And don't you know that for as long as my will lasts in you, so does the divine life

15
00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:14.880
last within you.

16
00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:21.000
And that as soon as my will ceases, so does the divine life cease, and you take back your

17
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:27.320
human life with all the problems that go with it."

18
00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:31.360
That's a beautiful exchange that you make, he said.

19
00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:36.280
The same happens with obedience for as long as the obedience lasts, so does the life of

20
00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:40.320
the one who commanded last in the one who obeys.

21
00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:46.520
But as soon as the obedience ceases, so does one take back one's own life.

22
00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:51.320
And then he tells her about the future, and I want to give you Amos 3, 7, that the Lord

23
