00:41:03.040 --> 00:41:08.720
course is the right-hand side of Christ, and flowing out right out into the arabah.

442
00:41:08.720 --> 00:41:17.280
The arabah is the desert-like place, transforming it into a fertile land."

443
00:41:17.280 --> 00:41:23.720
So these waters of grace flow into the desert of our souls and fertilize us them, making

444
00:41:23.720 --> 00:41:26.320
them fruitful spiritually.

445
00:41:26.320 --> 00:41:33.480
Now as creatures also practice the virtues, little springs are formed in their hearts.

446
00:41:33.480 --> 00:41:42.160
Now this is John 7 verses 37 to 39, where Jesus said, "Come and drink, and drink as much

447
00:41:42.160 --> 00:41:48.040
as you want, and eventually out of your own heart will flow fountains of living water.

448
00:41:48.040 --> 00:41:53.520
In other words, you become a source of life for other people."

449
00:41:53.520 --> 00:41:59.680
So as creatures also practice the virtues, little springs are formed in their hearts,

450
00:41:59.680 --> 00:42:05.720
from which their little rivulets gush forth, which cross with my rivulets, that's John

451
00:42:05.720 --> 00:42:12.360
14, 12, my disciples will do the same works as I do when I go to the Father.

452
00:42:12.360 --> 00:42:17.520
So as creatures also practice the virtues, little springs are formed in their hearts,

453
00:42:17.520 --> 00:42:23.360
from which their little rivulets gush forth, which cross with my rivulets, and spurting

454
00:42:23.360 --> 00:42:30.000
up together with mine glorify the celestial father and descend for the good of all, forming

455
00:42:30.000 --> 00:42:36.160
such harmony between heaven and earth that even the angels remain amazed at the enchanting

456
00:42:36.160 --> 00:42:37.920
sight.

457
00:42:37.920 --> 00:42:44.360
Therefore be attentive to practice the virtues of my sacred heart.

458
00:42:44.360 --> 00:42:51.320
So as to let me open the springs of my graces in you and through you.

459
00:42:51.320 --> 00:42:57.480
So that's Galatians 5-22 and we'll take a break there.
